  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-skill-hub",
      "text": "[中文版](README.zh.md) | [English](README.md)\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-skill-hub\"><img alt=\"npm version\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/npm/v/dsh-skill-hub?color=2f81f7&label=npm\"></a>\n  <img alt=\"downloads\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/npm/dm/dsh-skill-hub\">\n  <img alt=\"license\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/npm/l/dsh-skill-hub\">\n  <img alt=\"node\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/node-%3E%3D22.19-339933\">\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-skill-hub",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cheshireez/dsh-skill-hub/main/promo/real-skill-hub.png\" alt=\"dsh-skill-hub panel\" width=\"640\">\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-skill-hub",
      "text": "In-GUI skill hub for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) — manage the full `ctx.skills` catalog from the Web GUI. Beyond browsing, toggling and market installs, it puts the weight on two things other managers don't do: **audit before install** (hidden characters, remote-execution pipes, credential paths, size caps — a blocking finding is refused before it lands) and **budget after install** (the name + description characters of the first progressive-disclosure layer, so you learn at 8000 that a skill would install but never trigger)."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-skill-hub",
      "text": "> Host runs in the dsh process via official SDKs only; browser renders through official slots. No dsh source changes."
    },
    {
      "section": "Quick start",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-skill-hub"
    },
    {
      "section": "restart dsh web → Settings → 技能 → Market → scan → import",
      "text": "```\n\nRequires `Node ^22.19 || >=24` + dsh web `>=0.1.7-alpha.1 <0.3`. dsh `0.2.2` and later require `Node >=24.9`."
    },
    {
      "section": "restart dsh web → Settings → 技能 → Market → scan → import",
      "text": "Two surfaces — the hub panel lives at **Settings → 技能**, and this plugin's own configuration card sits on the plugin's page in the **Plugins manager** (sidebar → 插件 → dsh-skill-hub). The card is registered by the plugin itself into the `plugins.bundle.config` slot — dsh has no auto-generated config page — and covers the master switch, announce-to-agent, dot colors, usage display and the stats window/interval."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "**Settings → 技能** — 3 tabs: **Sources** (skills, flat/grouped + project tree), **Scenes** (custom tag groups), **Market** (install + update)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **Browse** — every root of the `ctx.skills` registry: project / user / bundled + third-party providers. Search across name, description, `displayName`; filter by source and invocation (model / user); sort by name, added time, or usage. Same-name skills from different sources get a duplicate badge instead of silently hiding.\n- **Content audit** — enabled skills' bodies (`SKILL.md`) are checked too: raw ESC control characters, Unicode tag characters, and bidirectional controls (these three make \"reviewed\" not equal \"seen\" — a market import carrying them is refused outright), zero-width characters, `curl … | sh` remote execution, SSH/cloud-credential/keychain paths, over-long descriptions, and the 2 MiB per-file / 10 MiB per-skill / 500-file limits. Pure local static matching: no model call, no network. A market import scans the whole bundle (including `scripts/`); the standing check only reads `SKILL.md` — it runs on every 5-second poll, and walking every directory would slow the panel down.\n- **Announcement budget** — the name + description total that the first progressive-disclosure layer injects comes back with the catalog, so the panel can show characters and an estimated token"
    },
    {
      "section": "Choosing between managers",
      "text": "Several skill managers exist in this ecosystem and they cover more ground than this one: [`@michengai/dsh-skills-manager`](https://github.com/MichengAI/dsh-skills-manager) adopts 20+ agent folders, aggregates both the ClawHub and skills.sh markets, and supports ZIP import and self-update; [dsh-skill-importer](https://github.com/saitamahang/dsh-skill-importer) / [dsh-find-skill](https://github.com/Moximxxx/dsh-find-skill) focus on import alone."
    },
    {
      "section": "Choosing between managers",
      "text": "This plugin's trade-off is to **go deep on what happens after something is installed**:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Choosing between managers",
      "text": "| What you want | Pick |\n| --- | --- |\n| Adopt as many agent folders as possible, ZIP import, multi-language UI | `@michengai/dsh-skills-manager` |\n| Just move skills over from another agent | `dsh-skill-importer` |\n| **The source is unknown (a random GitHub repo) and you want to see what is inside before installing** | this plugin |\n| **You keep installing skills and want to know when you cross the injection budget and start getting \"installed but never triggers\"** | this plugin |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Choosing between managers",
      "text": "| Capability | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| Content audit | Raw ESC / Unicode tag characters / bidirectional controls / zero-width characters / `curl … \\| sh` / SSH and cloud credential paths / 2 MiB per file, 10 MiB per skill, 500 files. A blocking finding refuses the write (a market import is refused as a whole and its temp directory removed); warnings are only flagged. Pure local static matching: no network, no model call. |\n| Announcement budget | The name + description total of the first progressive-disclosure layer comes back with the catalog, so the panel shows characters and an estimated token count; past 8000 it turns red — clients truncate the tail there, which shows up as \"installed but never triggers\". |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Choosing between managers",
      "text": "Scaffold format (`SKILL.md`):\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: my-skill\ndescription: One line when the agent should use this skill.\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "my-skill",
      "text": "Body...\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "```text\nGitHub repo ──scan/import──▶ ~/.dsh/skills\n     ▲                          │\n     └─check/sync/delete── ctx.skills ◀─ provider\n                                │ snapshot/get"
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "Host uses only `ctx.skills.snapshot/get`, `ctx.webServer.register`, `ctx.systemPrompt.section`. Routes sit behind dsh's own `/api` trust fence (loopback / the listener's bind address / `--trusted-host`), JSON; **write routes (POST) additionally require an `x-dsh-skill-hub: 1` header** — a cross-site page cannot forge a custom header, and a same-origin request skips the CORS preflight so it costs no extra round trip. The provider registers in the global skill layer and once more into every live agent's skill layer (nearer than the preset layer), so an invocation override can outrank the host's native entries."
    },
    {
      "section": "HTTP API",
      "text": "| Endpoint | Method | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `/api/skill-hub/catalog?cwd=` | GET | skills + disabled + diagnostics + duplicates |\n| `/api/skill-hub/skill?name=&cwd=` | GET | skill body (works for disabled too) |\n| `/api/skill-hub/skill/delete` | POST | move to trash (snapshots source+scenes) |\n| `/api/skill-hub/toggle` | POST | `{name, enabled}` |\n| `/api/skill-hub/toggle-batch` | POST | `{names, enabled}` |\n| `/api/skill-hub/create` | POST | `{name, description?, root?}` |\n| `/api/skill-hub/diagnostic/fix` | POST | `{path}` auto-fix frontmatter |\n| `/api/skill-hub/stats` | GET | invocation counts |\n| `/api/skill-hub/config` | GET/POST | runtime config (`null` clears) |\n| `/api/skill-hub/groups` | GET | tags + collections + orders |\n| `/api/skill-hub/tag` etc. | POST | create/rename, delete, set members, reorder |\n| `/api/skill-hub/market` etc. | GET/POST | list/add/delete/pin sources; `…/source/check` + `…/source/sync` update them |\n| `/api/skill-hub/market/source/versions?repo=` | GET | releases + branches for the version picker |\n| `/api/skill-hub/market/skills-sh?q=` | GET | skills.sh index search (server-side proxy, ≥2 chars; results validated as strict `owner/repo`) "
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```bash\nnpm run typecheck  # tsc --noEmit\nnpm test           # 420 tests, 23 suites\nnpm run build      # tsc + tsdown → lib/index.js + lib/client.js\n```\n\n> Don't run two `dsh web` on the same `$DSH_HOME` + cwd — no session-log lock (`seq gap` corruption). Use separate `DSH_HOME`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Troubleshooting",
      "text": "- `duplicate loader entry id: skill-hub` — remove the duplicate install (keep one `dsh plugin add` method).\n- Skill missing — check the diagnostics section (frontmatter / name mismatch / short description / two discovery forms claiming the same name: a `<name>/SKILL.md` bundle and a `<name>.md` file can coexist on disk, and the registry keeps only one of them).\n- Empty source group — its skills were deleted, or their disabled records were lost (sidecar restored/hand-edited). Startup reconciles `.disabled` files on disk **and prunes records whose file is gone** (a record left behind by a hand-deleted directory used to be un-actionable: enable, create and delete all failed). Source groups with no visible member are no longer rendered.\n- A skill cannot be created / stays \"disabled\" — the disabled record pointed at a file that no longer exists. At startup (and on the next enable attempt) the record is repointed at the surviving `.disabled` file, or dropped so the name is free again.\n- Dots missing in `/` menu — dsh internals changed; catalog still works.\n- Settings card missing — open the plugin in the Plugins manager (sidebar → 插件 → dsh-skill-hub) and expand the 「技能中枢」 card at the top"
    },
    {
      "section": "Community",
      "text": "[Issues](https://github.com/cheshireez/dsh-skill-hub/issues) · [Discussions](https://github.com/cheshireez/dsh-skill-hub/discussions) · [Showcase](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/3161) · [Market PR](https://github.com/awesome-dsh-plugin/awesome-dsh-plugin/pull/1746) · [Discord](https://discord.gg/Ycq5dCaS4)"
    },
    {
